WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.331
"The Benefits of Turmeric Curcumin for Arthritis,
Blood Sugar, Cholesterol, and Body Weight"

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.120
The number of clinical trials
on turmeric—

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.880
not in rats or Petri dishes—

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.240
but with actual people
continues to climb—

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.760
dozens a year,

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.600
and most were randomized,
double-blind,

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.800
placebo-controlled,

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.840
the gold standard
for clinical trials.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.600
There have been
so many trials published

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.880
that there are now
umbrella reviews on turmeric.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.600
You've heard of systematic
reviews and meta-analyses,

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.840
pooling multiple studies
together.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.480
Well, an umbrella review
can be like a systematic review

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.880
and meta-analysis
of systematic reviews

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.640
and meta-analyses,

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.760
meaning pooling multiple
meta-analyses together,

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.160
placing them at the very top
of the hierarchy

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.840
of evidence pyramid.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.440
Dr. Greger has covered
the benefits

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.200
of the turmeric pigment curcumin

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.360
for knee osteoarthritis,

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.840
in some cases working
as well as or even better

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.560
than anti-inflammatory drugs
and painkillers

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.920
without their side effects
of injuring our gut,

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.280
and in the ten years since,

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.760
a meta-analysis
of 11 meta-analyses

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.440
on the efficacy of curcumin
for relieving osteoarthritis

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.520
strongly supports
that it can relieve pain

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.520
as well as improve
joint mobility

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.920
and shorten medication use.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.400
And more isn't
necessarily better.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.160
Low-dose extracts
appear to have

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.920
similar pain relief effects
to high-dose extracts.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.560
What about other
arthritic conditions?

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.440
A pilot study in 2012
of 45 patients

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.760
showed promise
for rheumatoid arthritis,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.280
finding it is
actually more effective

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.480
at alleviating pain
compared to the leading drug.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:35.840
And a recent meta-analysis

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.520
including
more than 500 patients

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.120
found the same:

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.760
curcumin was beneficial
both for inflammation levels

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.520
and clinical symptoms.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:47.520
Curcumin's ability to lower
some inflammatory biomarkers,

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.120
like C-reactive protein,

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.440
a marker
of systemic inflammation,

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.880
extends more broadly
to patients

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.960
with autoinflammatory conditions

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.600
and the stronger effects
seemed to appear

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.480
at relatively smaller doses.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.280
You may recall that Dr. Greger
talked about a 2012 study

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.200
in prediabetic individuals

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.760
where zero percent of those
taking curcumin extract

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.560
for nine months progressed
to type 2 diabetes

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.400
while 16% of those
on placebo did.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.120
There have been
a lot of studies since.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.360
Fourteen systematic reviews
and meta-analyses

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.960
containing 61 individual
randomized controlled trials

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.840
were included
in this umbrella review.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.840
Fasting blood sugars and HbA1C,

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.000
a measure of longer-term blood
sugar control, both improved,

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.400
no matter what formulation
of turmeric or curcumin

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.160
was consumed,

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.800
but the quality
of the studies was low,

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.720
not including
important information

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.960
like their funding sources,

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.520
and the types of
turmeric/curcumin preparations

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.440
were wide ranging.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.400
What if we want to know
the impact of turmeric alone,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.400
not a special
curcumin formulation

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.320
that supplement companies
can charge us

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.480
a bunch of money for?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.080
This dose-response
meta-analysis

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.120
breaks it out for us

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.680
with turmeric resulting
in better results

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.360
than curcumin-only treatments.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:08.240
Note that benefit was found
for a variety of participants,

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.040
not only those with diabetes,

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.560
What about cholesterol?

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.560
Here's another umbrella review.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.840
Although the authors concluded

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.640
that curcumin could have
ameliorating effects,

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.920
there was only
a half-point drop in LDL.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.720
Lower doses may work better,
but a two-point drop

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.280
is still nothing
to write home about.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.760
Turmeric curcumin
"blocks obesity" in mice

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.520
fed a high-fat diet.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.200
What about people?

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.400
In an umbrella review of 50
randomized controlled trials,

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.920
curcumin supplementation
significantly decreased BMI,

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.720
body weight,
and waist circumference.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.640
It was significant
statistically,

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.320
but how much of a difference
did it really make?

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.320
A loss of about a half kilogram

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.280
or a little more than a pound
of body weight.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.000
Waist circumference,
a measure of abdominal obesity,

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.920
decreased by about a centimeter

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.600
and triple the effect in trials

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.360
with whole turmeric
relative to curcumin extracts.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.760
So, for those with obesity
or type 2 diabetes

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.600
and wanting to lose weight,

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.480
the primary prescription
is lifestyle modification,

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.880
and some turmeric on the side
might be helpful

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.741
but may not make
that much difference.

